--- OVERVIEW: Train_PPiMg2 ---

Synced from MareNostrum 5, /gpfs/scratch/uv36/adrian/deepmd-training/Train_PPiMg2, on
10/10/2026. This is the ArcaNN training area for the ppimg2 (2Mg(2+)[P2O7](4-)) system.

IMPORTANT -- WHY THE LFER FOLDERS ARE NOT HERE

On the cluster this directory also appears to contain 'LFER_3_mg2/' and
'NNP_LFER_choice/', but both are SYMLINKS into ../LFER/, not directories. The duplicate
copies that used to sit here were merged into the single trees under LFER/ on 02/10 and
07/10/2026 and then deleted (884 GB and 121 GB recovered). In this repo that content
lives under 'LFER/' only, so it is not duplicated here either. See docs/STRUCTURE_OVERVIEW.md
section 3.1, and LFER/README.

The symlinks are kept on the cluster because 159 scripts hardcode the old
'Train_PPiMg2/LFER_3_mg2' path and 1830 hardcode 'Train_PPiMg2/NNP_LFER_choice', almost
all of them to reach the NNP graph files. Editing through either spelling edits the same
file. The two rsync scripts that used to maintain the mirror are retired on the cluster
('copy_LFER_3_mg2.sh.retired_20261002', 'verify_LFER_3_mg2.sh.retired_20261002') and must
not be run: with the symlink in place their source and destination resolve to the same
directory.

WHAT IS ACTUALLY HERE

o Simulations/       NNP-driven MD of ppimg2 on the ArcaNN iteration-006 committee,
                     separate from the PMF machinery. 'prod_MD/' is a single reference
                     production run; 'TS_OPES/' is OPES exploration of the TS region.
                     Read TS_OPES/README before using it: of the five replica folders,
                     rep1 and rep2 are complete, rep3 is partial and rep4/rep5 are
                     empty, so an analysis globbing 'rep*' averages over two. Those are
                     being kept deliberately, not cleaned.

o initial_dataset/   generation of the pre-iteration-0 DeePMD training set: CP2K AIMD,
                     frame extraction, CP2K labeling, conversion to DeePMD format. Two
                     generations -- the top-level repN were extracted with VMD, which
                     truncated coordinate decimals and distorted structures (CP2K "atom
                     closer than 0.5 A"), so rep3-rep8 were discarded; 'new_rep/' is the
                     script-based re-extraction and is the live data. See its 'README.md'
                     for the layout and 'README.txt' for the author's own notes and the
                     per-replica configuration counts.

Only scripts, summary tables and READMEs are kept here. The per-frame 'Energy_000NN.txt'
extractions (about 3400 files) and the raw CP2K per-configuration job dirs stay on the
cluster, following the same curation rule as arcann_workflow/ -- see that folder's README.
The DeePMD-format dataset itself ('new_rep/init_mg2ppi-initial/', .raw plus set.000/*.npy)
is also cluster-only; .npy is gitignored.
